# Electronics

## What the Circuit Does

This is a DC motor control circuit. A small microcontroller (ATtiny25) reads two buttons and uses them to turn a motor on and off. The motor runs on 24V while the microcontroller runs on 3.3V.

## Main Parts

- **ATtiny25 microcontroller** — the brain of the circuit, controls everything
- **MOSFET (Q1)** — acts as a switch that turns the motor on and off based on the microcontroller's signal
- **Motor (M1)** — the DC motor being controlled
- **Zener diode (D1)** — protects the circuit from voltage spikes when the motor stops
- **Two push buttons (SW1, SW2)** — used by the user to start and stop the motor
- **Sense resistor and voltage divider** — lets the microcontroller monitor how much current the motor is drawing
- **Decoupling capacitors** — filter out electrical noise on both power rails
